      </h2>
      <p>
        Commercial kitchens use these four low-cost garnishes to elevate a 50-cent slice into a luxury restaurant dessert presentation:
      </p>

      <ul style="padding-left: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 2rem; line-height: 1.8;">
        <li><strong>Fresh Organic Raspberry & Mint Leaf (15¢):</strong> Place one plump raspberry and a fresh baby mint leaf against the side of each slice.</li>
        <li><strong>Warm Raspberry Coulis Drizzle (10¢):</strong> Spoon a clean culinary curve of strained raspberry puree across the dessert plate.</li>
        <li><strong>Edible Gold Leaf Flakes (8¢):</strong> Use culinary tweezers to apply a microscopic fleck of 24k edible gold leaf to the top crust.</li>
        <li><strong>Micro Edible Flowers (12¢):</strong> Pansies, violas, or borage blossoms provide an upscale garden-aesthetic finish.</li>
      </ul>

